[00:00.000 --> 00:11.000]  There is something that is very very interesting, we have three three phase wire coils powered by this variable frequency device which is only 500 watts in total.
[00:11.000 --> 00:17.000]  Below that we put a 70 millimeter magnet there with a 14 millimeter hole in the middle.
[00:17.000 --> 00:24.000]  And just to hold it up we put a 60 millimeter magnet here which repels it and just hold it up in place.
[00:24.000 --> 00:37.000]  Now as we add a rotating magnetic field to that central magnet it will start going downward toward the repulsive magnet.
[00:37.000 --> 00:59.000]  And as that happens the central rod above will lift up as a Newtonian third law reaction to the other magnet pushing down.
[00:59.000 --> 01:07.000]  And there it's just falling out because it lifted up so high. Let's do the same experiment the weight on the pole above so that it can't move.
[01:07.000 --> 01:16.000]  We start off at low power spinning in the Newtonian domain till about 12 hertz.
[01:16.000 --> 01:21.000]  The magnet is trying to go downward is pushing the pole upward if it could.
[01:21.000 --> 01:31.000]  We go to 15 hertz, 25 hertz, it rises up like a top.
[01:31.000 --> 01:42.000]  And now there's no Newtonian force in the rod at all just hovering there freely in space.
[01:42.000 --> 01:59.000]  If we take it down again, say to 12 hertz you can see the rod lifting up.
