[00:00.000 --> 00:07.000]  No space to put the magnet in the floor.
[00:07.000 --> 00:22.040]  Today we will show how the Hamdi Ukar levitation experiment of 2021 may be
[00:22.040 --> 00:23.960]  somewhat artificial.
[00:30.000 --> 00:37.000]  The two magnets will just attract one another as expected.
[00:37.000 --> 00:44.000]  If we spin the North Pole on the magnet, nothing happens.
[00:44.000 --> 00:50.000]  The same attraction, one magnet spinning at 5000 rpm,
[00:50.000 --> 00:54.000]  other one remains stationary.
[00:54.000 --> 00:56.000]  Next we will do something different.
[00:56.000 --> 01:04.000]  We will make the magnet on the Horazontal, so that the red North Pole is perpendicular to the magnet.
[01:04.000 --> 01:15.000]  Now when we put it close, again we get an attraction simply by NS to SN magnetic dipole interactions.
[01:15.000 --> 01:18.000]  Nothing special has happened yet.
[01:18.000 --> 01:21.000]  Finally when we have that Horazontal magnet on a magnet,
[01:21.000 --> 01:28.000]  we spin it at 5000 rpm.
[01:28.000 --> 01:37.000]  The other magnet will spin quite rapidly.
[01:37.000 --> 01:45.000]  The key point here however is that when the Horazontal magnet is spinning on the
[01:45.000 --> 01:52.000]  Dremel, it attracts the other magnet.
[01:52.000 --> 01:59.000]  It does not float, it sticks right to the magnet, it does space between them.
[01:59.000 --> 02:03.000]  You can follow a lot of gravity to make it float to half.
[02:03.000 --> 02:08.000]  It is just a normal, very tight interaction.
[02:08.000 --> 02:13.000]  The idea that we can study this phenomenon using permanent magnets is incorrect.
