[00:00.000 --> 00:04.960]  The first thing I notice about the spinning gyroscope is that it resists the
[00:04.960 --> 00:10.160]  temps to change its position. A resistive force appears when I attempt to tilt or
[00:10.160 --> 00:16.640]  rotate the gyro. Now when I stand it on the tabletop it stays vertical. The
[00:16.640 --> 00:22.280]  spinning wheel is creating a force that holds the gyroscope upright. When the wheel
[00:22.280 --> 00:27.280]  stops the force disappears and the gyroscope falls.
[00:32.280 --> 00:38.960]  Incredibly this force will support the gyroscope like this. It appears to be
[00:38.960 --> 00:56.360]  levitating. A spinning gyroscope will balance on a string.
[01:08.960 --> 01:13.960]  You can even lift the gyroscope with a string looped around one end.
