[00:00.000 --> 00:06.000]  Ultimately, the easiest way to see how a gyroscope maintains its orientation is with a three-axis gimbal.
[00:06.000 --> 00:11.000]  This gimbal allows the gyroscope to spin on all three axes.
[00:11.000 --> 00:19.000]  So, if the gyroscope starts in one orientation, no matter how much we turn the rest of the gimbal, or what it's sitting on,
[00:19.000 --> 00:22.000]  the gyroscope will keep pointing in the same direction.
[00:22.000 --> 00:27.000]  This is the same gimbal that Feynman used when he was teaching.
